(tests/test_defensive_engines.py contains seven test_* methods and asserts that) Tj T*
(the manual registry contains 22 entries. The test suite was not executed during) Tj T*
(this review. No pass/fail result or coverage percentage is claimed.) Tj T*
(Additional phase-verification scripts exist; their execution was not reproduced.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. ENGINEERING DECISIONS AND TRADE-OFFS) Tj T*
(Async event dispatch supports multiple consumers but increases concurrency complexity.) Tj T*
(SQLite keeps evidence storage local and self-contained; distributed use needs more design.) Tj T*
(Canonical JSON plus SHA-256 helps detect changes on re-verification; it is not a) Tj T*
(replacement for digital signatures or immutable external storage.) Tj T*
(Thread-to-async bridging integrates blocking workers but adds lifecycle complexity.) Tj T*
(Linux iptables enforcement provides native control but reduces cross-platform portability.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. FINDING) Tj T*
(The inspected Event Bus _safe_dispatch catches handler exceptions and currently) Tj T*
(uses pass. This isolates subscriber failures but does not provide visible logging) Tj T*
(in that method. Structured exception logging and failure metrics are recommended.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. ROADMAP) Tj T*
(Execute tests in a controlled environment; add structured event logging; inventory) Tj T*
(and pin dependencies; benchmark precision, recall and false positives; obtain an) Tj T*
(independent security review before making certification claims.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
